## Implementation

- Commit: 534f9ec4102ab6efb3948db79d825c21aa838747
  `docs(storytime): check the image in the flag runbook (track_id: storytime_app_rebuild_20261025)`.
  Files: `docs/runbooks/storytime-deploy.md` and `__tests__/phase4-runbook.test.ts` (a
  Green-owned file). No adversarial test file changed. No production source changed, so the
  browser gate and build-graph were not needed; tsc still ran as a guard for the edited test
  file and exited 0.
- Runbook rewrite (the flag section of `storytime-deploy.md`):
  - A new bullet states the defect: a services update builds the new revision from the
    template of the latest revision, not from the revision that serves the traffic, and the
    build workflow deploys every push with `--no-traffic`, so the latest revision can be a
    build that Daniel has not approved.
  - A new code block reads the traffic split and the image of the live revision before the
    flag commands:
    `gcloud run services describe storytime-app --project primary-advantage --region asia-southeast1 --format='value(status.traffic)'`
    and
    `gcloud run revisions describe <live revision> --project primary-advantage --region asia-southeast1 --format='value(status.imageDigest)'`.
  - Both flag commands now carry `--image=<the live revision image digest>`, `--no-traffic`,
    and a tag (`--tag=teacher-flag-on`, `--tag=teacher-flag-off`), with the service, the
    project, and the region, and keep `--update-env-vars` and `--remove-env-vars`.
  - The words "traffic-neutral" are gone. A new bullet says the commands do not keep the
    traffic place by themselves and hold no traffic only because of `--no-traffic`.
  - A new bullet sends the operator to the tag URL of the new revision before the traffic
    step (`/th/teacher/2/1` answers 200 with a teacher session and the flag on, 404 with the
    flag off), names the revision list command, and keeps Daniel's go for the traffic step.
- Test extension (`phase4-runbook.test.ts`, 4 to 7 cases): both flag command lines must hold
  `--image=`, `--no-traffic`, and `--tag=`; the section must hold the two live-revision read
  commands; the section must hold no "traffic-neutral", must tag the revision, must name the
  tag URL check, and must keep Daniel's go. The positive control for the `--set-env-vars`
  check stays.
- Two fix-ups during the round: the prose no longer holds the literal phrase
  "gcloud run services update" outside a code block (the committed F461 case extracts the
  first match up to a backtick and read the prose), and the negated "traffic-neutral"
  sentence is reworded, so the phrase holds nowhere in the document.

